From 02bf82a5bc41dd764afc4054ce45cf07ebd87704 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Williams <alexis@typedr.at>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] Call more callbacks through their own function types

Calling a function through a pointer to a type with a different
parameter list or return type is undefined behaviour; WebAssembly
checks the type of every indirect call and traps with "function
signature mismatch". These sites were missed by the earlier fixes:

- gtypemodule: GTypeModule's class_init took one argument, so every
  GIO extension point (and any GTypeModule) trapped on first use.
- gbookmarkfile: g_bookmark_file_copy() passed g_strdup() and one-
  argument copy functions to g_list_copy_deep() as GCopyFunc.
- gsourceclosure: g_closure_ref(), which returns the closure, was the
  void-returning ref function of a closure source's callback funcs.
- gdbusinterfaceskeleton, gdbusobjectmanagerserver, gdbusobjectproxy,
  gdbusobjectskeleton, gmemorymonitorbase, and the interface init
  functions gdbus-codegen emits: one-argument GInterfaceInitFunc.
- gtester: g_free() passed to g_slist_foreach() as a GFunc.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Wasm-specific]
